<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Communist Party of Nepal (Unified Marxist–Leninist)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1991–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as CPN (UML), CPN-UML</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-nepal-maoist-centre">Communist Party of Nepal</a> (Unified Marxist–Leninist) is one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>'s largest parties, formed in 1991 by the merger of two communist parties that had joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/1990-peoples-movement">1990 People's Movement</a>. Its leader Man Mohan Adhikari formed a minority government in 1994, and it has since led several governments, most often under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/k-p-sharma-oli">K. P. Sharma Oli</a>. It briefly merged with the Maoists as the Nepal Communist Party from 2018 to 2021.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-nepal-unified-marxist-leninist.jpg" alt="Communist Party of Nepal (Unified Marxist–Leninist)" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CPN-UML · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_CPN-UML_(2021-).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
